## 2. Tactical Stance & Engine Execution (3,572 Recorded Decisions)

V3's matrix exhibits the highest sustained reliance on $W$ utility moves across the entire roster without sacrificing ground pressure or special finisher throughput.

```
                 ACTION DISTRIBUTION (SOUL Tier — 1,233 Decisions)
  Forward / Push (D)  [####################################### ] 43.9% (541 uses)
  Special Finisher (S)[######################                  ] 25.2% (311 uses)
  Utility / Belt (W)  [#################                       ] 19.3% (238 uses) 🌪️
  Idle / Recover      [#######                                 ] 7.9%  (97 uses)
  Retreat / Guard (A) [###                                     ] 3.7%  (46 uses)

```

### Key Tactical Findings

1. **`W+L` Utility Engine Monopolization (84%–87% of $W$ Actions):**
* **SOUL Tier:** 200 out of 238 $W$ actions were **`W+L`** (84.0%).
* **MASTER Tier:** 95 out of 109 $W$ actions were **`W+L`** (87.2%).
* **EASY Tier:** 116 out of 139 $W$ actions were **`W+L`** (83.5%).
`ForeseeEngine` routinely initiates setup sequences with `W+L` (Double Typhoon Buff), using the state advantage to amplify follow-up physical and special sequences.


2. **`D+L` Sweep Combo Dominance ($\sim 76\%–80\%$ of $D$ Actions):**
* Out of 541 physical attacks in SOUL tier, **420 were `D+L**` (77.6%). V3 uses `D+L` as his undisputed neutral ground poke, providing reliable damage output and steady Chi generation.


3. **`S+L` & `S+J` Dual Special Finisher Strategy:**
* Unlike Nigo (who spams 3-Chi `S+J`) or Ichigo (who hoards for 9-Chi `S+I`), V3 splits special spend evenly between **`S+L`** (131/311 in SOUL) and **`S+J`** (113/311 in SOUL). This dual-tier cash-out maintains constant pressure while preventing Chi cap waste.



